    "text_blocks": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "The best time to take a vitamin B12 supplement is first thing in the morning on an empty stomach with water.",
        "snippet_highlighted_words": [
          "first thing in the morning on an empty stomach with water"
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          0
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Why Morning is Ideal"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Energy support: Vitamin B12 plays a key role in energy metabolism and red blood cell production. Taking it early helps align with your body's natural rhythm.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              1,
              2
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Avoid sleep issues: Taking B12 late in the afternoon or evening can overstimulate your nervous system and cause restlessness or trouble sleeping."
          }
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          0
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Empty Stomach vs. With Food"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Empty stomach: As a water-soluble vitamin, B12 is best absorbed when taken without food (about 30 minutes before a meal or two hours after).",
            "snippet_links": [
              {
                "text": "water-soluble vitamin",
                "link": "https://health.clevelandclinic.org/the-best-time-to-take-vitamins"
              }
            ],
            "reference_indexes": [
              3,
              4
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "With food alternative: If you have a sensitive stomach or experience mild nausea, taking it with a light breakfast is completely fine and will not ruin your results."
          }
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          0
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Key Tips for Consistency"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Consistency matters most: The most crucial factor is taking your supplement at the same time every day to maintain steady levels, as your body does not store water-soluble vitamins long-term.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              2,
              5
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Pair with a habit: Tie your supplement routine to a morning habit, like drinking your first glass of water or brushing your teeth.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              2
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Spacing out other supplements: If you take calcium supplements, keep them separate from your morning B12, as high amounts of calcium can hinder B12 absorption. Always consult a doctor to confirm your proper dosage, especially if you follow a plant-based diet or have a known deficiency."
          }
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          2,
          6,
          7
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "If you'd like, share:"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Your dietary preferences (vegan, vegetarian, or omnivore)"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Any symptoms you are experiencing"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "I can help you understand if a supplement is right for you or what dosage is typically suggested."
      }
